# Codex Adapter Rules

All Codex platform knowledge lives under `src/adapters/codex/`. Never add `.codex/` paths, TOML keys, or version checks to `src/core/`.

## Version matrix

- All version-sensitive behavior goes through `src/adapters/codex/version/matrix.ts`.
- Every non-trivial resolver rule needs a matrix entry and a fixture.
- Features without matrix entries resolve as `unknown`.

## Discovery (read-only)

- Never write to the scanned project's `.codex/**`.
- Only external process allowed in normal scan: `codex --version`.
- Untrusted projects: skip project `.codex/` layers (config, hooks); user config still loads.
- Redact TOML `env` and secrets — key names only.

## Facts corpus

- Verified facts: [docs/CODEX-FACTS.md](../../docs/CODEX-FACTS.md)

## When uncertain

Return `unknown` with a reason. Trust unreadable → `unknown`, not `blocked`.
